{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a40a8cd5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003548,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.627399+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.623851+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Chest X-ray Classification (Normal vs Abnormal) — Transfer Learning with DenseNet121\n","\n","**What changed compared with the from-scratch version**\n","\n","| | From scratch (before) | This notebook |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| Model | 5-block custom CNN, random init | **DenseNet121 pre-trained on ImageNet** (swappable: ResNet50V2, EfficientNetB0, …) |\n","| Training | 1 phase | **2 phases**: train new head → fine-tune top of the backbone |\n","| Class imbalance | class weights | **Synthetic minority-class images** (training split only) |\n","| Data split | `take`/`skip` on a reshuffling dataset (images can drift between splits) | **Fixed, stratified file-level split** (70 / 20 / 10) |\n","| Preprocessing | `/255` (applied twice by accident) | **Backbone-specific preprocessing inside the model** |\n","| Evaluation | accuracy, confusion matrix | + ROC-AUC, sensitivity/specificity, classification report, **Grad-CAM** |\n","\n","> **Kaggle note:** downloading ImageNet weights needs **Internet = On** in the notebook settings\n","> (Settings → Internet). Alternatively, attach the Keras weights file as a dataset.\n","\n","**Label convention:** `Normal = 0`, `Abnormal = 1`. Abnormal is the \"positive\" class, so *recall* = sensitivity to disease."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0bff9607","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002673,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.633551+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.630878+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Setup & configuration"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"0a77e33f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.640309Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.639858Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.075773Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.074556Z"},"papermill":{"duration":23.441454,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.077516+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:51:48.636062+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["TensorFlow 2.20.0 | Keras 3.13.2\n","GPUs: [PhysicalDevice(name='/physical_device:GPU:0', device_type='GPU'), PhysicalDevice(name='/physical_device:GPU:1', device_type='GPU')]\n"]}],"source":["import os, shutil, random, warnings\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import tensorflow as tf\n","from tensorflow import keras\n","from tensorflow.keras import layers\n","from PIL import Image\n","from scipy.ndimage import gaussian_filter, map_coordinates\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","from sklearn.metrics import (confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay,\n","                             classification_report, roc_curve, roc_auc_score)\n","\n","warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n","print(\"TensorFlow\", tf.__version__, \"| Keras\", keras.__version__)\n","\n","gpus = tf.config.list_physical_devices(\"GPU\")\n","for gpu in gpus:\n","    tf.config.experimental.set_memory_growth(gpu, True)\n","print(\"GPUs:\", gpus)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"1ccbcb09","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.084709Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.0841Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.091385Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.090723Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.012617,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.092868+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.080251+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# ───────── Configuration (edit here) ─────────\n","DATA_DIR   = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/lyesaitk/cnn-project-dataset/Model_Dataset_2/Model_Dataset_2\"\n","OUT_DIR    = \"/kaggle/working\" if os.path.isdir(\"/kaggle/working\") else \"./outputs\"\n","os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","CLASS_NAMES = [\"Normal\", \"Abnormal\"]       # label 0 = Normal, label 1 = Abnormal (positive class)\n","\n","BACKBONE    = \"densenet121\"                 # \"densenet121\" | \"resnet50v2\" | \"efficientnetb0\" | \"vgg16\"\n","WEIGHTS     = \"imagenet\"                    # None = random init (only useful for debugging)\n","\n","IMG_SIZE    = (224, 224)\n","BATCH_SIZE  = 32\n","SEED        = 42\n","\n","EPOCHS_HEAD = 5        # phase 1: backbone frozen, only the new head trains\n","EPOCHS_FINE = 15       # phase 2: top of the backbone unfrozen (early stopping will cut this short)\n","LR_HEAD     = 1e-3\n","LR_FINE     = 1e-5\n","FINE_TUNE_LAST = 120   # number of backbone layers to unfreeze in phase 2 (BatchNorm stays frozen)\n","\n","keras.utils.set_random_seed(SEED)\n","AUTOTUNE = tf.data.AUTOTUNE"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e9ca5c5a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002469,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.09847+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.096001+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 2. Load file list and make a fixed, stratified split\n","\n","The original notebook split a `tf.data` pipeline with `take`/`skip`. That pipeline reshuffles every time it is\n","iterated, so images near the split boundaries can move between train/val/test from one pass to the next.\n","Here the split is done **once, on file paths**, stratified by class, so every image lives in exactly one split."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"a9b5274d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.104801Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.104441Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.970266Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.969283Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.871159,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.972168+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:12.101009+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Folders found: ['Abnormal', 'Normal']\n","Normal    -> label 0 |  10192 images\n","Abnormal  -> label 1 |  11941 images\n","    Lung_Opacity           6012\n","    Pneumonia              5929\n","train:  15493 images | Normal= 7134  Abnormal= 8359\n","val  :   4426 images | Normal= 2038  Abnormal= 2388\n","test :   2214 images | Normal= 1020  Abnormal= 1194\n"]}],"source":["VALID_EXT = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".bmp\"}\n","\n","print(\"Folders found:\", os.listdir(DATA_DIR))\n","all_paths, all_labels = [], []\n","for label, name in enumerate(CLASS_NAMES):\n","    folder = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, name)\n","    files = []\n","    for root, _, fnames in os.walk(folder):          # walks into sub-folders too\n","        for f in sorted(fnames):\n","            if os.path.splitext(f)[1].lower() in VALID_EXT:\n","                files.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n","    files.sort()                                      # deterministic order -> reproducible split\n","    all_paths  += files\n","    all_labels += [label] * len(files)\n","    print(f\"{name:9s} -> label {label} | {len(files):6d} images\")\n","\n","    # breakdown per sub-folder (e.g. Pneumonia / Lung Opacity)\n","    sub = {}\n","    for p in files:\n","        key = os.path.relpath(os.path.dirname(p), folder)\n","        sub[key] = sub.get(key, 0) + 1\n","    if len(sub) > 1 or \".\" not in sub:\n","        for k, v in sub.items():\n","            print(f\"    {k:20s} {v:6d}\")\n","\n","# 70 % train / 20 % val / 10 % test, stratified\n","train_paths, tmp_paths, train_labels, tmp_labels = train_test_split(\n","    all_paths, all_labels, test_size=0.30, stratify=all_labels, random_state=SEED)\n","val_paths, test_paths, val_labels, test_labels = train_test_split(\n","    tmp_paths, tmp_labels, test_size=1/3, stratify=tmp_labels, random_state=SEED)\n","\n","for name, y in [(\"train\", train_labels), (\"val\", val_labels), (\"test\", test_labels)]:\n","    y = np.array(y)\n","    print(f\"{name:5s}: {len(y):6d} images | Normal={np.sum(y==0):5d}  Abnormal={np.sum(y==1):5d}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"67b45812","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.980029Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.979184Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.073931Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.072971Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.103479,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.078704+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:13.975225+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 2000x400 with 6 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Quick look at a few real images\n","rng_vis = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n","idx = rng_vis.choice(len(train_paths), 6, replace=False)\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 6, figsize=(20, 4))\n","for ax, i in zip(axes, idx):\n","    ax.imshow(Image.open(train_paths[i]).convert(\"L\"), cmap=\"gray\")\n","    ax.set_title(CLASS_NAMES[train_labels[i]]); ax.axis(\"off\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0c062726","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004898,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.089374+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.084476+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3. Synthetic image generation to balance the classes\n","\n","Abnormal is the minority class. I generate new Abnormal images until the **training set is balanced**.\n","\n","**How the synthetic images are made** — each one starts from a random *real, training-split* Abnormal image and gets a\n","random combination of:\n","- a small **geometric warp** (rotation ±10°, shift ±5 %, zoom 0.92–1.08) plus a smooth **elastic deformation**\n","- **intensity changes** (gamma, contrast, brightness)\n","- light **sensor noise** and optional slight blur\n","\n","Design choices that matter for medical images:\n","- **No horizontal flips** — flipping a chest X-ray moves the heart to the right side, which is anatomically wrong.\n","- Borders are filled by **edge replication**, not black, so the model can't learn \"black corners = synthetic\".\n","- Synthetic images are made **only from training images** and are **only added to the training set**.\n","  Validation and test stay 100 % real, so the reported metrics are not inflated."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"433988da","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.100881Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.100271Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.111301Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.110695Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.018474,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.112814+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.09434+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def random_warp(img, rng, max_rot=10, max_shift=0.05, zoom=(0.92, 1.08),\n","                elastic_px=2.0, elastic_sigma=8):\n","    \"\"\"Rotation + shift + zoom + elastic deformation in ONE resampling step. img: float32 [H,W] in 0..1\"\"\"\n","    h, w = img.shape\n","    yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(h), np.arange(w), indexing=\"ij\")\n","    cy, cx = (h - 1) / 2, (w - 1) / 2\n","\n","    theta = np.deg2rad(rng.uniform(-max_rot, max_rot))\n","    s = rng.uniform(*zoom)\n","    ty, tx = rng.uniform(-max_shift, max_shift, 2) * np.array([h, w])\n","\n","    y0, x0 = yy - cy - ty, xx - cx - tx                      # output -> input (inverse mapping)\n","    xs = ( np.cos(theta) * x0 + np.sin(theta) * y0) / s + cx\n","    ys = (-np.sin(theta) * x0 + np.cos(theta) * y0) / s + cy\n","\n","    for field in (\"dx\", \"dy\"):                                # smooth random displacement field\n","        d = gaussian_filter(rng.standard_normal((h, w)), elastic_sigma)\n","        d = d / (d.std() + 1e-8) * elastic_px\n","        if field == \"dx\": xs = xs + d\n","        else:             ys = ys + d\n","\n","    return map_coordinates(img, [ys, xs], order=1, mode=\"nearest\")\n","\n","\n","def random_intensity(img, rng):\n","    gamma = rng.uniform(0.80, 1.25)\n","    img = np.clip(img, 0, 1) ** gamma\n","    mean = img.mean()\n","    img = (img - mean) * rng.uniform(0.85, 1.15) + mean + rng.uniform(-0.05, 0.05)\n","    if rng.random() < 0.5:\n","        img = gaussian_filter(img, rng.uniform(0.3, 0.7))\n","    img = img + rng.normal(0, rng.uniform(0.0, 0.02), img.shape)\n","    return np.clip(img, 0, 1)\n","\n","\n","def make_synthetic(path, rng):\n","    img = Image.open(path).convert(\"L\").resize(IMG_SIZE[::-1], Image.BILINEAR)\n","    arr = np.asarray(img, dtype=np.float32) / 255.0\n","    arr = random_intensity(random_warp(arr, rng), rng)\n","    return Image.fromarray((arr * 255).astype(np.uint8), mode=\"L\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"304e8cc8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.124149Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.123411Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.571592Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.570731Z"},"papermill":{"duration":105.460711,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.578381+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:52:15.11767+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Training counts: {'Normal': np.int64(7134), 'Abnormal': np.int64(8359)}\n","Minority class: Normal -> generating 1225 synthetic images\n","Saved 1225 synthetic images to /kaggle/working/synthetic_Normal\n"]}],"source":["counts = np.bincount(train_labels)\n","minority = int(np.argmin(counts))\n","n_needed = int(counts.max() - counts.min())\n","print(f\"Training counts: {dict(zip(CLASS_NAMES, counts))}\")\n","print(f\"Minority class: {CLASS_NAMES[minority]} -> generating {n_needed} synthetic images\")\n","\n","SYNTH_DIR = os.path.join(OUT_DIR, f\"synthetic_{CLASS_NAMES[minority]}\")\n","shutil.rmtree(SYNTH_DIR, ignore_errors=True)\n","os.makedirs(SYNTH_DIR)\n","\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n","minority_train = [p for p, y in zip(train_paths, train_labels) if y == minority]\n","sources = rng.choice(len(minority_train), n_needed, replace=n_needed > len(minority_train))\n","\n","synth_paths, pairs = [], []\n","for k, src_idx in enumerate(sources):\n","    src = minority_train[src_idx]\n","    out = os.path.join(SYNTH_DIR, f\"synth_{k:05d}.png\")\n","    make_synthetic(src, rng).save(out)\n","    synth_paths.append(out)\n","    if k < 6: pairs.append((src, out))\n","print(f\"Saved {len(synth_paths)} synthetic images to {SYNTH_DIR}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"b763e96e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.590105Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.589443Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.359244Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.358465Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.789138,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.37267+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:00.583532+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1920x660 with 12 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Original (top) vs synthetic (bottom)\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, len(pairs), figsize=(3.2 * len(pairs), 6.6))\n","for j, (src, syn) in enumerate(pairs):\n","    axes[0, j].imshow(Image.open(src).convert(\"L\").resize(IMG_SIZE[::-1]), cmap=\"gray\"); axes[0, j].axis(\"off\")\n","    axes[1, j].imshow(Image.open(syn), cmap=\"gray\");                                     axes[1, j].axis(\"off\")\n","axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Real (source)\", loc=\"left\"); axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Synthetic\", loc=\"left\")\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"904ae3ff","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.402642Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.402062Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.54253Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.541809Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.15784,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.54482+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.38698+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Balanced training counts: {'Normal': np.int64(8359), 'Abnormal': np.int64(8359)}\n"]}],"source":["# Final training set = real train + synthetic minority images.  Val / test are untouched.\n","train_paths_bal  = train_paths + synth_paths\n","train_labels_bal = train_labels + [minority] * len(synth_paths)\n","\n","before, after = np.bincount(train_labels), np.bincount(train_labels_bal)\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 4))\n","x = np.arange(2); w = 0.38\n","ax.bar(x - w/2, before, w, label=\"Before\"); ax.bar(x + w/2, after, w, label=\"After (with synthetic)\")\n","ax.set_xticks(x); ax.set_xticklabels(CLASS_NAMES); ax.set_ylabel(\"Training images\"); ax.legend()\n","ax.set_title(\"Training-set class balance\"); plt.show()\n","print(\"Balanced training counts:\", dict(zip(CLASS_NAMES, after)))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f7675775","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.012829,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.571337+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.558508+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4. Input pipeline\n","Images are fed as raw `0–255` floats. The **backbone-specific normalisation lives inside the model** (next section), so training,\n","evaluation and inference can never get out of sync."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"00426050","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.600084Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.599557Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.268833Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.268192Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.685953,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.270691+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:01.584738+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["WARNING: All log messages before absl::InitializeLog() is called are written to STDERR\n","I0000 00:00:1792785242.050992      23 gpu_device.cc:2020] Created device /job:localhost/replica:0/task:0/device:GPU:0 with 13756 MB memory:  -> device: 0, name: Tesla T4, pci bus id: 0000:00:04.0, compute capability: 7.5\n","I0000 00:00:1792785242.055196      23 gpu_device.cc:2020] Created device /job:localhost/replica:0/task:0/device:GPU:1 with 13756 MB memory:  -> device: 1, name: Tesla T4, pci bus id: 0000:00:05.0, compute capability: 7.5\n"]}],"source":["def load_image(path, label):\n","    raw = tf.io.read_file(path)\n","    img = tf.io.decode_image(raw, channels=3, expand_animations=False)   # grayscale -> 3 channels\n","    img.set_shape([None, None, 3])\n","    img = tf.image.resize(img, IMG_SIZE)                                  # float32, 0..255\n","    return img, label\n","\n","def make_dataset(paths, labels, training):\n","    ds = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices((np.array(paths), np.array(labels, dtype=np.float32)))\n","    if training:\n","        ds = ds.shuffle(len(paths), seed=SEED, reshuffle_each_iteration=True)\n","    ds = ds.map(load_image, num_parallel_calls=AUTOTUNE).batch(BATCH_SIZE)\n","    return ds.prefetch(AUTOTUNE)\n","\n","train_ds = make_dataset(train_paths_bal, train_labels_bal, training=True)\n","val_ds   = make_dataset(val_paths,  val_labels,  training=False)\n","test_ds  = make_dataset(test_paths, test_labels, training=False)   # no shuffling -> predictions line up with test_labels"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"30cc3211","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.013529,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.298886+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.285357+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5. Model — pre-trained backbone + new classification head\n","\n","**Why DenseNet121 as the default?**\n","- It is the architecture behind **CheXNet**, the well-known chest-X-ray model, so it has a strong track record on exactly this modality.\n","- Dense connections reuse features across layers, which works well on subtle textures (lung opacity, infiltrates) and is parameter-efficient (~7M backbone params).\n","- It fine-tunes reliably with small learning rates and modest GPUs (a Kaggle T4 is plenty).\n","\n","Alternatives are one config change away (`BACKBONE = ...`): **ResNet50V2** (robust baseline), **EfficientNetB0** (smallest/fastest), **VGG16** (heavy, mostly for comparison).\n","AlexNet is not available in `keras.applications` and is outdated compared with all of the above.\n","\n","Architecture: `augmentation (train only) → preprocessing → backbone → GlobalAveragePooling → Dropout → Dense(1, sigmoid)`"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"7e123fbe","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.328061Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.327347Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T19:54:07.984556Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T19:54:07.983818Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.674173,"end_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:07.986254+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T19:54:04.312081+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Downloading data from https://storage.googleapis.com/tensorflow/keras-applications/densenet/densenet121_weights_tf_dim_ordering_tf_kernels_notop.h5\n","\u001b[1m29084464/29084464\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m0s\u001b[0m 0us/step\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<pre style=\"white-space:pre;overflow-x:auto;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo,'DejaVu Sans Mono',consolas,'Courier New',monospace\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold\">Model: \"clifford_densenet121\"</span>\n","</pre